You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the law. These terms do not limit them.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any license to anyone else, or to prevent the licensor from granting licenses to anyone else. These terms do not impair any right the licensor has of its own.

## Patent Defense

If you make any legal claim against anyone accusing the software, with or without changes, of infringing any patent, then all licenses granted to you for the software under these terms end immediately. If you make any legal claim against anyone accusing changes you make to the software, or new works based on the software, of infringing any patent, then all licenses granted to you for changes you make to the software under [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license) end immediately.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing that you have violated any of these terms, or that you violated [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license) under [Patent Defense](#patent-defense), your licenses from the licensor for the software and changes to the software resume, if you do both of the following:

1.  Stop the violation within thirty days of the notification.

2.  Ensure that each person who had a right to notice under [Notices](#notices) and did not receive it gets notice, also within thirty days of the notification.

If you don't do both of these things, your licenses end immediately and permanently. To get licenses again, you must get a new license from the licensor.

